{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>And He said.</b> HaShem said to His heart or to the angels." "<b>I will hide.</b> After the manner of human language, and likewise 'I will close My eyes.' The meaning: when they seek Me, they will not find help." "<b>I will see what their end is.</b> Some say: I will hide My face from them because I see what they will do in the end. The correct interpretation is the plain sense: until I see what they will do when distress comes upon them." "<b>For a generation of reversals.</b> Joined to 'I will hide My face.'" "<b>Reversals.</b> Who turned to serve Elohim other than Me — and they were My children, for I begot them. And behold, there is no אמונה in them, and it is a noun or an adjective, for there is in them no man of אמונים, for we find that 'the faithful fail' opposite 'the devout,' likewise 'keeper of faithfulness.'"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:26:00.757395552Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}